## 1. STRICT RULES & ARCHITECTURE (MANDATORY)

### 1.1 CSS-First Architecture & Zero Inline CSS
- **No Inline CSS:** The `style="..."` attribute is forbidden anywhere in the HTML. Zero exceptions.
- **Class Selectors Only:** All design properties, layout rules, and states are applied via class (BEM) or ID selectors in `style.css`.
- **Minimal HTML Modifications:** HTML stays semantic and styling-agnostic. Changing the site's entire look must only require editing `style.css`, never the markup.

### 1.2 CSS Variables & Theme Tokens
- **Token Completeness:** `:root` must contain every mandatory token from 0.5. Components must reference tokens (`var(--...)`) — no hard-coded colors in component rules. The only permitted literal colors: the two opaque glass-fallback values (0.6), and `#0d2a4a` for the Vista-white input text/placeholder.
- **Contrast Pairing (enforced for every theme):** Light backgrounds pair with dark text tokens; dark backgrounds pair with light text tokens. Dark theme: `#f3faff` text on navy/glass. Light theme: `#0d2a4a` text on pale-sky/glass. Verify pairing holds in both themes.
- **Light-Mode Background:** Never pure white. The light theme uses a pale sky-blue mood gradient (see 1.3). Where a near-white solid is truly needed, use `#fefefe`, never `#ffffff`.
- **Theme-Conditional Decorations:** The button `text-shadow` (and any other color-dependent decoration) applies in the dark theme only; remove it in the light theme to protect contrast.

### 1.3 Mandatory Dark Mode Support
- **Mechanism:** Dark tokens are the `:root` default. Light tokens are defined twice: under `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light) { :root:not(.dark) { ... } }` (so no-JS users follow system preference) and under `:root.theme-light { ... }` (explicit override). A `.dark` class on `<html>` forces dark.
- **Light Token Values (starting points — verify ≥ 4.5:1 contrast and adjust if needed):**
  `--primary: #1e63b8; --secondary: #3d8eeb; --bg-primary: #dff0fb; --bg-secondary: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); --surface-strong: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); --text-primary: #0d2a4a; --text-secondary: rgba(13,42,74,0.75); --text-success: #146c43; --text-error: #b3261e; --border-default: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); --border-success: rgba(20,108,67,0.6); --border-error: rgba(179,38,30,0.6); --bg-image: radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% -20%, #f4fbff 0%, #dff0fb 55%, #bcd9ee 100%); --glass-fill: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.85) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.5) 45%, rgba(214,234,250,0.35) 100%); --glass-sheen: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,0.95) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.3) 40%, rgba(255,255,255,0) 70%); --shadow-sm: 0 2px 6px rgba(13,42,74,0.18); --shadow-md: 0 8px 24px rgba(13,42,74,0.2), 0 0 12px rgba(61,142,235,0.25); --shadow-lg: 0 20px 50px rgba(13,42,74,0.25), 0 0 24px rgba(61,142,235,0.3); --shadow-inset-hi: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.95);`
- **Persistence:** On load, `script.js` reads `localStorage.getItem('aero-theme')`; `'light'` → add `.theme-light`; `'dark'` → add `.dark`; absent → do nothing (the media query governs). Every toggle writes the choice back. Because the CSS default already matches system preference, no flash-of-wrong-theme occurs without inline scripts.
- **Toggle Control:** A visible `.theme-toggle` button in the nav, containing Material Symbols `light_mode` / `dark_mode`, with `aria-pressed` (true when dark is active) and a dynamically updated `aria-label` ("Switch to dark theme" / "Switch to light theme"). The icon swap must not change the button's dimensions.

### 1.4 Flexbox Layout & Mobile-First Alignment
- **Flex Everywhere:** Build all layout structures (nav, section headers, card rows, form rows, footer columns) with `display: flex`.
- **Default Alignment Rule:** Every flex container defaults to `align-items: center` unless an exception is explicitly justified in a CSS comment. Justified exceptions on this page: card/plan/step rows on desktop use `align-items: stretch` for equal-height panels; footer link columns use `flex-start` for top-aligned text.
- **Mobile-First:** All rows are single-column flex by default and become multi-column at `min-width: 768px` / `min-width: 1024px` breakpoints. No horizontal scrolling at any viewport down to 320px. All interactive targets ≥ 44×44px.

### 1.5 Styling Approach
- Use **clean custom CSS** in a single `style.css`, organized with native CSS `@layer` in this order: `tokens`, `base`, `layout`, `components`, `states`, `utilities`. Do not load Tailwind or any CSS framework, and do not mix styling conventions.

### 1.6 Typography & Icons (Google Fonts Mandatory)
- **Text:** Load **Open Sans** (weights 400, 600, 700, 800) and **Roboto Mono** (400, 700) via Google Fonts `<link>` tags (with `preconnect`), bound to `--font-base`, `--font-display`, and `--font-mono`.
- **Icons:** Use **Google Material Symbols (Rounded variant)** via its stylesheet, invoked with ligature names (e.g., `<span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">speed</span>`). Raw inline SVGs and local icon files are forbidden.
- **Exception (Segoe UI):** The source theme requests Segoe UI/Tahoma/Consolas, which are OS-local fonts not hosted on Google Fonts — they may appear only as fallbacks inside the font stacks in 0.5; the primary fonts must be the Google Fonts above (Open Sans approximates Segoe UI; Roboto Mono approximates Consolas).

