## 3. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES (GLOBAL)

- **Responsive by Default:** Fluid type (clamp headings), responsive breakpoints, zero horizontal overflow at 320px+.
- **Smooth Animations:** Apply `transition: transform var(--transition-fast) var(--ease-standard), box-shadow var(--transition-fast) var(--ease-standard)` (or `var(--transition-normal)` for larger surfaces) to every state change. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` — disable float/tilt/cascade animations and `scroll-behavior: smooth`; keep instant, non-transformative state changes. Respect `prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce` per 0.6.
- **Accessibility:** Body text ≥ 4.5:1 and large text ≥ 3:1 contrast in **both** themes against the *composited* glass background — if a glass panel holds dense text, add a subtle solid scrim layer inside it via an extra background layer. Never rely on color alone. Use semantic HTML5 landmarks (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `footer`), exactly one `<h1>` (hero) with logical heading order, a visually-hidden-until-focused skip link to `#main`, correct ARIA on all custom widgets, logical DOM/focus order, and full keyboard operability — no mouse-only interactions anywhere. Announce dynamic feedback (form errors, loading, success) through `aria-live` regions.
- **Mandatory Visual Feedback:** Every interactive element (nav links, footer links, buttons, FAQ triggers, theme toggle, plan buttons) responds visibly to hover and focus (glow, sheen shift, underline, or transform).
- **Destructive Actions:** None exist on this page — do not invent any.
- **Anchor Navigation:** `scroll-behavior: smooth` with `scroll-margin-top` on sections to offset the sticky nav.

